Z||000005||Old Lar||05-12-2000||09:21 PM||||When you add aftermarket items to your car you are personalizing it.  That means you do what ever you want.  Not everyone will agree with your choices.<BR>Do you like it? There are over 1000 members on the forum.  If 51% like it, you've got a winner.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 05-12-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000006||Flash Box||05-12-2000||09:36 PM||||Old Lar I agree as long as I like it then what the heck. I figured though some of you guys and gals have probably done been through the trial and error part on what works and what doesn't. ||||reg||7
Z||000007||frontal lobe||05-13-2000||01:00 AM||||Hi Flash Box!  Welcome.  The impression I have found on the forum overall is that the majority of guys love the looks of the exterior the way it is.  I've only even seen a FEW exterior mods.  I've seen a few guys change the headlights.  A few have modified the air intake.  A couple have done a few things to the hood and deck.<P>Most of the modification talked about is under the hood.  A little in the interior.<P>Knock yourself out.  It's your car.  Keep us posted.  Most people are VERY nice and if they don't like what you do, won't rip you.  If you ask for opinions, some will directly answer if they don't like it, but won't insult you!||||reg||1
